implementationPlan.description:
The sh fix, in scripts/moe-agent.sh.

1. An idle_wait SECONDS helper, defined before the grouped main loop next to the INT/TERM trap:
   idle_wait() { local rc=0; sleep "$1" || rc=$?; [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || echo "[WARN] MOE_IDLE_WAIT_INTERRUPTED: the ${1}s wait ended early (sleep exited $rc); the seat keeps looping." >&2; return 0; }
   Its comment says why. A sleep killed by another process used to end the seat under set -e (five seats on 2026-10-31 at 04:47Z). The wrapper's own Ctrl+C, SIGINT or SIGTERM still stops it: bash runs the INT/TERM trap's `exit 0` as soon as the sleep returns, before `||` is evaluated. Probed for this plan: SIGTERM to the shell, then to its sleep, gave 'stopped' and exit 0, with no `||` branch; a killed sleep alone gave 'interrupted rc=143' and the script continued.
2. Use idle_wait for every idle or backoff wait:
   - sleep "$POLL_INTERVAL" (the idle poll);
   - sleep "$LAUNCH_FAIL_BACKOFF_SEC" (the launch-failure and outage backoff);
   - sleep "$MOE_TASKLESS_POLL_SEC" (the single-shot taskless wait);
   - the account lease loop's sleep "$trust_sec" (untrusted retry) and sleep "$f1" (MOE_ACCOUNT_WAIT).
   Leave the sub-second retries and the heartbeat sidecar alone: its subshell already runs `set +e`.
3. cleanup_temp, the EXIT trap:
   - its very first statement is `local exit_status=$?`, ahead of `set +e`;
   - the deregister sends reason terminal_closed when exit_status is 0, else unexpected_exit:<status>;
   - for a non-zero status it also prints one best-effort line to stderr: `[WARN] seat exiting with status <N>; deregistering as unexpected_exit:<N>`.
   These stay unchanged:
   - the INT/TERM trap still ends in `exit 0`, so Ctrl+C and SIGTERM keep terminal_closed;
   - the hot-reload hand-over keeps its explicit wrapper_restart;
   - a hang-up stays untrapped: it runs the EXIT trap with the last command's status, normally 0 (probed). The JetBrains plugin also deregisters a closed tab as terminal_closed itself (MoeProjectService.kt).
   The daemon stores any reason string up to 200 chars (deregisterWorker.ts), so no daemon change is needed (DoD 2).
Then `bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh`, and step 1's arm passes.
Error handling: the EXIT trap stays best-effort under set +e, so a failed echo or moe-call never aborts it. idle_wait always returns 0, so a set -e abort can only come from somewhere else.
